      {
       "id": "w7",
       "task": "dialog",
       "image": "",
       "attackers": [],
       "reward_exp": 0,
       "description": "<i>Bandits rob whoever the road brings them. These men were placed on the one road one woman has to take, days before she took it.</i> <br> <br> <i>And a shut waystation still has a road under it. Somebody has spent a year standing on that road taking what the station used to take, and writing none of it down. An open door at the top of the pass ends that on the first morning.</i> <br> <br> <i>The posting said bandits. The posting was wrong. And the rule on every slip is plain: a false posting frees the escort. You may turn back now, paid for the road you walked, with no fault written against you.</i> <br> <br> <i>The keeper has not stopped walking.</i> <br> <br> \"I wrote bandits. Bandits is what I could afford.\"",
       "reward_rank": "NONE",
